+<a name="rfc.section.5.3"></a><h3>5.3.&nbsp;
+Media Type Registration</h3>
+
+<a name="MediaContents"></a><br /><hr />
+<table summary="layout" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="2" class="TOCbug" align="right"><tr><td class="TOCbug"><a href="#toc">&nbsp;TOC&nbsp;</a></td></tr></table>
+<a name="rfc.section.5.3.1"></a><h3>5.3.1.&nbsp;
+Registry Contents</h3>
+
+<p>
+	    This section registers the
+	    <tt>application/logout+jwt</tt>
+	    media type <a class='info' href='#RFC2046'>[RFC2046]<span> (</span><span class='info'>Freed, N. and N. Borenstein, &ldquo;Multipurpose Internet Mail Extensions (MIME) Part Two: Media Types,&rdquo; November&nbsp;1996.</span><span>)</span></a> in the IANA "Media Types"
+	    registry <a class='info' href='#IANA.MediaTypes'>[IANA.MediaTypes]<span> (</span><span class='info'>IANA, &ldquo;Media Types,&rdquo; .</span><span>)</span></a> in the manner
+	    described in <a class='info' href='#RFC6838'>[RFC6838]<span> (</span><span class='info'>Freed, N., Klensin, J., and T. Hansen, &ldquo;Media Type Specifications and Registration Procedures,&rdquo; January&nbsp;2013.</span><span>)</span></a>, which can be used to
+	    indicate that the content is a Logout Token.
+	  
+</p>
+<p> 
+	  </p>
+<ul class="text">
+<li>
+	      Type name: application
+	    
+</li>
+<li>
+	      Subtype name: logout+jwt
+	    
+</li>
+<li>
+	      Required parameters: n/a
+	    
+</li>
+<li>
+	      Optional parameters: n/a
+	    
+</li>
+<li>
+	      Encoding considerations: binary;
+	      A Logout Token is a JWT;
+	      JWT values are encoded as a
+	      series of base64url-encoded values (some of which may be the
+	      empty string) separated by period ('.') characters.
+	    
+</li>
+<li>
+	      Security considerations: See <a class='info' href='#CrossJWT'>Section&nbsp;4.1<span> (</span><span class='info'>Cross-JWT Confusion</span><span>)</span></a> of this specification
+	    
+</li>
+<li>
+	      Interoperability considerations: n/a
+	    
+</li>
+<li>
+	      Published specification: <a class='info' href='#LogoutToken'>Section&nbsp;2.4<span> (</span><span class='info'>Logout Token</span><span>)</span></a> of this specification
+	    
+</li>
+<li>
+	      Applications that use this media type:
+	      Applications that use Logout Tokens to achieve back-channel logout
+	    
+</li>
+<li>
+	      Fragment identifier considerations: n/a
+	    
+</li>
+<li>
+	      Additional information:
+<blockquote class="text">
+<p>Magic number(s): n/a
+</p>
+<p>File extension(s): n/a
+</p>
+<p>Macintosh file type code(s): n/a 
+</p>
+</blockquote>
+	      <br />
+
+	    
+</li>
+<li>
+	      Person &amp; email address to contact for further information:
+	      <br />
+
+	      OpenID Foundation Artifact Binding Working Group - openid-specs-ab@lists.openid.net
+	    
+</li>
+<li>
+	      Intended usage: COMMON
+	    
+</li>
+<li>
+	      Restrictions on usage: none
+	    
+</li>
+<li>
+	      Author: OpenID Foundation Artifact Binding Working Group - openid-specs-ab@lists.openid.net
+	    
+</li>
+<li>
+	      Change controller: OpenID Foundation Artifact Binding Working Group - openid-specs-ab@lists.openid.net
+	    
+</li>
+<li>
+	      Provisional registration? No
+	    
+</li>
+</ul><p>
+	  
+</p>
